# ============================================================
# .trivyignore — Accepted CVE suppressions for Trivy
# ============================================================
# ── Go stdlib CVEs (gosu + Grafana binaries) ────────────────────────────────
# These CVEs are in Go standard library code compiled into gosu and Grafana
# binaries. They are NOT present in our Java Spring Boot service images.
#
# For gosu (postgres:15-alpine / redis:alpine):
#   The gosu maintainers confirm these CVEs do not apply because gosu does
#   not invoke the affected code paths (net/mail, html/template, httputil,
#   HTTP/2 transport). Reference: github.com/tianon/gosu/issues/104.
#
# For Grafana (grafana/grafana:13.1.1 as of 2026-07-31, third-party monitoring):
#   Grafana is a monitoring dependency, not part of the application attack
#   surface. Bumped 12.4.6 -> 13.1.1 to clear ~25 flagged CVEs at once
#   (854b8b7); the Go-stdlib entries below are left suppressed until the
#   next CI Trivy scan confirms which ones the new image already resolved —
#   GitHub auto-resolves code-scanning alerts that no longer reproduce, no
#   manual dismissal needed for genuinely-fixed ones.
#
# CVE-2026-33811 — net: CNAME double-free/DoS via long CNAME response (cgo DNS).
#   gosu: does not make cgo DNS queries.
#   Java images: not affected (JVM DNS, not Go net).
CVE-2026-33811
# CVE-2026-33814 — golang.org/x/net: HTTP/2 SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE=0 infinite loop.
#   gosu: does not use HTTP/2 transport.
#   Java images: not affected (use Netty/Tomcat, not Go x/net).
CVE-2026-33814
# CVE-2026-39820 — net/mail: ParseAddress/ParseAddressList/ParseDate excessive CPU.
#   gosu: does not parse RFC 5322 email addresses.
CVE-2026-39820
# CVE-2026-39836 — net: panic in Dial/LookupPort on NUL byte (Windows only).
#   Containers run on Linux Alpine; Windows code path is unreachable.
CVE-2026-39836
# CVE-2026-42499 — net/mail: consumePhrase quadratic DoS.
#   gosu: does not parse email headers.
CVE-2026-42499
# CVE-2026-27142 — html/template: URL not escaped in meta content attribute (XSS).
#   gosu: does not render HTML templates.
#   Grafana: fix requires rebuild with Go ≥ 1.26.3; accepted upstream.
CVE-2026-27142
# CVE-2026-39825 — net/http/httputil: ReverseProxy forwards invisible query params.
#   gosu: does not use httputil.ReverseProxy.
#   Grafana: accepted upstream.
CVE-2026-39825
# CVE-2026-39826 — html/template: script type="" escaper bypass (XSS).
#   gosu: does not render HTML templates.
#   Grafana: accepted upstream.
CVE-2026-39826
# CVE-2026-39823 — html/template: URL not escaped in meta content attribute (XSS),
#   same family as CVE-2026-27142 above.
#   gosu: does not render HTML templates.
#   Grafana: fix requires rebuild with Go ≥ 1.26.3; accepted upstream.
CVE-2026-39823
# CVE-2026-42504 — mime: decoding a crafted MIME header with many invalid
#   encoded-words can consume excessive CPU (DoS).
#   gosu: does not decode MIME headers.
#   Grafana: accepted upstream pending release with Go ≥ 1.26.4.
CVE-2026-42504
# ── gosu Go stdlib CVEs, batch 2 (found 2026-09-10 after docker/postgres/Dockerfile
#   gained its own `apk upgrade`, which made hotel-pms/postgres:ci actually get
#   scanned instead of the bare upstream postgres:15-alpine tag — see ci.yml's
#   trivy job). All 16 are in usr/local/bin/gosu's bundled Go 1.24.6 stdlib.
#   gosu's entire job is: parse UID/GID args, setuid/setgid, execve the real
#   command — no network I/O, no TLS, no HTTP, no HTML/XML rendering, no cert
#   chain building. None of these code paths are reachable from that.
CVE-2025-68121
CVE-2025-61726
CVE-2025-61729
CVE-2026-25679
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32283
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-39822
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862
# ── postgres:15-alpine / redis:alpine — native library CVEs ─────────────────
# These are CVEs in Alpine OS packages bundled with the official upstream
# images, not in our application code. Both docker/postgres/Dockerfile and
# docker/redis/Dockerfile now run `apk update && apk upgrade --no-cache` on
# top of the base tag, which resolves any CVE with a patched Alpine package
# already published (confirmed: redis:8.8.2-alpine scans at 0 vulnerabilities
# post-upgrade). The two entries below are reachability-based exceptions —
# libraries present but not exercised by any code path we use — not "wait for
# upstream to rebuild the tag".
#
# CVE-2026-6732 — libxml2: type confusion / crash when validating a crafted
#   document against an XML Schema Definition (XSD) with an internal entity
#   reference. PostgreSQL's xml type (xpath/xmlparse) does not invoke XSD
#   schema validation (xmlSchemaValidateDoc) — that code path is not reachable
#   through any SQL-exposed function.
CVE-2026-6732
# CVE-2026-45447 — OpenSSL libssl3: use-after-free in PKCS7_verify() when
#   verifying a crafted PKCS#7/S-MIME signed message with an empty
#   digestAlgorithms ASN.1 SET. Neither PostgreSQL's nor Redis's use of
#   OpenSSL (TLS connection handshake only) calls PKCS7_verify() or any
#   PKCS#7/S-MIME message-signing API.
CVE-2026-45447
# ── Spring Cloud Config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CVE-2026-41002 — Spring Cloud Config Server TOCTOU on Git clone base dir.
#   config-service is internal-only (not routed through API gateway, T-CFG-01).
#   Protected by HTTP Basic Auth (T-CFG-03). No external exposure.
#   Affected: spring-cloud-config-server 5.x. Fix pending Spring Cloud 2025.x patch.
CVE-2026-41002
# ── Grafana (usr/share/grafana/bin/grafana) ──────────────────────────────────
# CVE-2026-21728, CVE-2026-28377 — grafana/tempo Go module, vendored into the
#   grafana binary for its Tempo datasource client. Both advisories concern the
#   Tempo *server* (DoS via large queries, S3 key leak via status endpoint);
#   we run no Tempo server and the Tempo datasource is not provisioned. Fix only
#   ships upstream (grafana 13.2.3 is not clean either: other bundled plugins).
#   Re-check on the next grafana patch bump.
CVE-2026-21728
CVE-2026-28377
# CVE-2026-97031, CVE-2026-78667 — Go stdlib (published 2026-10), fixed in Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2+.
#   Found in the grafana binary (go1.26.6) and its bundled datasource plugins (go1.26.7).
#   No grafana image carries the fix yet: checked 2026-10-09, 13.1.7 and 13.2.3 (latest stable,
#   2026-09-29) are still on go1.26.6/1.26.7 and `nightly` (13.3.0) is on go1.27.1 with plugins
#   on 1.26.7. Only a grafana rebuild can fix them, so a tag bump does not help.
#   CVE-2026-97031 — crypto/tls: a crafted ClientHello with several ECH outer-extension
#     references exhausts server memory. Only a TLS *server* with Encrypted Client Hello keys
#     configured is affected; grafana here serves plain HTTP (no TLS, no ECH).
#   CVE-2026-78667 — net/http: Range header with many small ranges makes FileServer/ServeContent
#     burn CPU. Grafana's static assets go through that path, so this one is reachable, but the
#     impact is a CPU DoS of the monitoring UI only (no data access): grafana runs in the opt-in
#     `observability` profile, needs a login for everything but static files, and
#     docker-compose.prod.yml unpublishes its port (only :80/:8080 are exposed).
#   Tracked as DEP-CVE-15 in THREAT_MODEL.md.
#   REMOVE BOTH when a grafana/grafana release built with Go >= 1.26.9 exists (check tags newer
#   than 13.2.3) and docker-compose.yml is bumped to it.
CVE-2026-97031
CVE-2026-78667
# Format: one CVE-ID per line, with a comment explaining the
# justification — mirrors the approach used in
# config/dependency-check/suppressions.xml for OWASP DC.
# ============================================================
